Phase 6A §4: complete test pyramid, run and verify.

`scripts/test_pyramid_report.py` (the single automated command) was built
to run every layer in one go, batching the integration layer internally
with memory-aware waits. It was run twice; both times the harness's own
external memory-pressure killer stopped the background process right at
the start of the integration layer (host free memory measured 0.48-0.82GB
at the time, from the user's own other applications -- same real,
recurring host instability documented throughout this phase). This is a
real, disclosed limitation of running the single command unbatched inside
one long-lived process on this specific host: the script's own internal
psutil-based wait loop cannot see or prevent an external OS-level kill of
the whole process.

The counts below were therefore produced by running the same batches the
script would have run, as separate tool invocations instead of one long
background job -- identical real pytest commands, identical real test
files, just issued one batch at a time so a kill (if any) only costs one
batch, not the whole run. Zero kills this time; all batches completed.

