FAILED: test_corpus_processing.py::test_real_corpus_has_no_genuinely_scanned_pdf_pages
This is a real, pre-existing finding about the real downloaded corpus
(data/raw/), NOT a regression introduced by this phase's work -- confirmed
by direct investigation: of 403 real PDFs / 6226 real pages in data/raw,
363 pages across 22 files (all in data/raw/ibbi/2026/, file mtimes dated
2026-10-31, before this Phase 6A session began) now genuinely need OCR,
where a prior run of this same test found zero. The test's own docstring
says exactly this: "If this ever fails, it means a real scanned page
finally showed up, which is useful to know, not a bug." No code in this
phase touched PDF/OCR extraction or added any file to data/raw/. Left as
a disclosed, real, open finding -- not fixed here (out of this phase's
scope; the real OCR path itself is already proven separately by
tests/test_ocr_engine.py's synthetic fixture).

